// Gablewick A: the land, the one source for both the terrain art and the collision mask.
//
// World pixels, y down. Each block is a closed chain of cubic Béziers (here straight lines: two
// control points at the thirds, then the end), run clockwise on screen: the roofs as walkable `Top`s
// left to right, then `Rock` down the walls (which stand past the map's bottom, in the canal) and
// back. A taller house's eave overhangs a lower neighbour's roof. Roofs are barely roughened
// (`rough: 0.2`): tiles, not rock. `dress` places decorations into the map's terrain.svg, one rule
// per slot (`{{name}}`); windows and doors are placed by hand, house by house, since a scatter would
// not line them up.
//
// A, "stepped": roofs alternate high and low toward a clock tower in the middle, the big cover. Spawns
// are mirrored about x = 950 (130, 395, 610, 830 and 1070, 1290, 1505, 1770). Alleys between the
// blocks drop to the canal.
Land(
    size: (1900, 1000),
    islands: [
        // Mill House: a tall house on the west edge, its gable low. One spawn (130).
        (
            start: (-42.0, 481.0),
            edges: [
                Top((8.7, 473.7), (59.3, 466.3), (110.0, 459.0)),
                Top((160.7, 466.3), (211.3, 473.7), (262.0, 481.0)),
                Rock((262.0, 483.3), (262.0, 485.7), (262.0, 488.0)),
                Rock((258.0, 488.7), (254.0, 489.3), (250.0, 490.0)),
                Rock((250.0, 673.3), (250.0, 856.7), (250.0, 1040.0)),
                Rock((156.7, 1040.0), (63.3, 1040.0), (-30.0, 1040.0)),
                Rock((-30.0, 856.7), (-30.0, 673.3), (-30.0, 490.0)),
                Rock((-34.0, 489.3), (-38.0, 488.7), (-42.0, 488.0)),
                Rock((-42.0, 485.7), (-42.0, 483.3), (-42.0, 481.0)),
            ],
            rough: 0.2,
        ),
        // Baker's Row: a low house (spawn 395) under the bakery's taller gable (spawn 610).
        (
            start: (278.0, 689.0),
            edges: [
                Top((317.0, 683.0), (356.0, 677.0), (395.0, 671.0)),
                Top((430.0, 676.4), (465.0, 681.8), (500.0, 687.2)),
                Rock((500.0, 621.4), (500.0, 555.7), (500.0, 490.0)),
